WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.602 --> 00:00:07.602
Not listening, but learning. For that is what everything is about in the Word of God.

2
00:00:07.602 --> 00:00:18.602
The Bible is incredibly powerful when you practice it and useless if you do nothing with it.

3
00:00:18.602 --> 00:00:20.602
It's that simple.

4
00:00:22.602 --> 00:00:26.602
This month we will speak openly about relationships.

5
00:00:27.602 --> 00:00:37.602
Why? Because I do not want to hold back on all the truths from the kingdom of God, from the Bible.

6
00:00:40.602 --> 00:00:53.602
There is so much wisdom to be gathered. There is so much you can find. Thousands of books. Thousands of websites.

7
00:00:54.602 --> 00:01:07.602
When it comes to relationships, dating, families, sexuality, pornography, which you received an email about from me last week.

8
00:01:07.602 --> 00:01:20.602
There is so much opinion being shot into the world, that I believe if the church keeps silent, the church is also being useless.

9
00:01:21.602 --> 00:01:30.602
So we need to have a loud voice in this world. We need to take responsibility upon ourselves.

10
00:01:32.602 --> 00:01:38.602
And it is so amazing to be able to talk today about the topic of parenting.

11
00:01:39.602 --> 00:01:48.602
Parenting is actually, as you may have heard two weeks ago, two weeks ago we spoke about family.

12
00:01:48.602 --> 00:01:54.602
And parenting and that first week of family are of course very closely related.

13
00:01:54.602 --> 00:02:02.602
Certain things overlap with each other. The composition of the family is part of parenting.

14
00:02:03.602 --> 00:02:07.602
The authority within the family is also part of parenting.

15
00:02:08.602 --> 00:02:24.602
So what I want to say first today is that in parenting, it primarily revolves around, parents, your personal relationship with God.

16
00:02:25.602 --> 00:02:32.602
You can say to yourself, okay, how am I going to raise my children without a relationship with God?

17
00:02:32.602 --> 00:02:43.602
But if you realize that He is the creator of children, who better to turn to for how you can raise your children?

18
00:02:45.602 --> 00:02:52.602
And the other thing I have to say about this is that parenting is not a theory or wisdom that you apply.

19
00:02:53.602 --> 00:02:54.602
And oh look, it works.

20
00:02:55.602 --> 00:03:04.602
Parenting has to do with your personal relationship with God, which is also reflected in your personal relationship with your children.

21
00:03:06.602 --> 00:03:16.602
Imagine you are walking through the house and you are a completely godless person and you actually have nothing to do with God, what do you communicate to your child?

22
00:03:17.602 --> 00:03:33.602
That can still be love, but I know about myself, so I won't say anything about you all, but I know about myself that if I had not had the love of God, my heart would not produce much more than just misery.

23
00:03:34.602 --> 00:03:41.602
Can a person love outside of Christ? Of course, but all love still comes from Christ.

24
00:03:42.602 --> 00:03:50.602
But it is about that recognition, it is about that affirmation, it is about recognizing God in everything, who you are and why you are and why life is.

25
00:03:51.602 --> 00:03:56.602
The Bible says, love for God is the beginning of all wisdom.

26
00:03:57.602 --> 00:04:04.602
So when you think to yourself, how should I raise my child? It starts with loving God.

27
00:04:05.602 --> 00:04:12.602
Vanessa and I love God and my children see everything I do.

28
00:04:13.602 --> 00:04:17.602
They literally see everything I do.

29
00:04:18.602 --> 00:04:22.602
They hear everything I say, the conversations I have with Vanessa.

30
00:04:23.602 --> 00:04:32.602
Sometimes I have adult conversations and then suddenly Joshua reacts, while he is sitting there eating, he responds to it and then oh my, he is listening in.

31
00:04:33.602 --> 00:04:36.602
They are sponges, our children.

32
00:04:37.602 --> 00:04:42.602
So the Bible also says where the heart is full, there the mouth speaks.

33
00:04:43.602 --> 00:04:55.602
So if there is something that my child receives as a primary sponge, it is still all the things that I simply say.

34
00:04:56.602 --> 00:05:03.602
My daily communication in life is what my child absorbs full-time.

35
00:05:04.602 --> 00:05:08.602
My child is always with me and receives everything I say.

36
00:05:09.602 --> 00:05:14.602
Even if I am at the checkout and I am paying money to the cashier and I give her a friendly greeting.

37
00:05:15.602 --> 00:05:16.602
Joshua, Olivia hear it.

38
00:05:17.602 --> 00:05:21.602
Even if I see a police officer on the street and I am respectful towards authority.

39
00:05:22.602 --> 00:05:24.602
Joshua and Olivia see it and hear it.

40
00:05:25.602 --> 00:05:30.602
Even if I am at home and it is not Sunday and I give glory to God in my own house.

41
00:05:31.602 --> 00:05:34.602
Joshua and Olivia hear and see it.

42
00:05:35.602 --> 00:05:36.602
So here you go already.

43
00:05:37.602 --> 00:05:40.602
Suppose I would never talk about God.

44
00:05:41.602 --> 00:05:45.602
Suppose I would never express my love for the Lord in my home circle.

45
00:05:46.602 --> 00:05:50.602
And I would only be focused on raising my child properly.

46
00:05:51.602 --> 00:05:53.602
Then you are already missing the point right away.

47
00:05:53.602 --> 00:05:59.602
Because it is important that your children know that there is a God who loves me.

48
00:06:00.602 --> 00:06:02.602
And that I give my love back to the Lord.

49
00:06:03.602 --> 00:06:05.602
Because my child imitates everything I do.

50
00:06:06.602 --> 00:06:09.602
I get angry, Joshua learns how to be angry.

51
00:06:10.602 --> 00:06:14.602
I say sorry to Vanessa, Joshua also learns how to say sorry to Olivia.

52
00:06:15.602 --> 00:06:17.602
By the way, these are my children for those who didn't know that yet.

53
00:06:18.602 --> 00:06:19.602
So your child imitates everything.

54
00:06:20.602 --> 00:06:21.602
It's your mini-me.

55
00:06:22.602 --> 00:06:25.602
It's who you are, what you have brought forth.

56
00:06:26.602 --> 00:06:27.602
That is what follows you around.

57
00:06:29.602 --> 00:06:31.602
And I prefer that they imitate me rather than the world. Amen.

58
00:06:34.602 --> 00:06:37.602
So it starts, my very first remark is.

59
00:06:38.602 --> 00:06:42.602
Your parenting begins with your love for God.

60
00:06:43.602 --> 00:06:45.602
Let's not lay any wisdom on the table just yet.

61
00:06:45.602 --> 00:06:49.602
There are still no instructions on how to approach this and how to approach that.

62
00:06:50.602 --> 00:06:53.602
It starts with your love for God.

63
00:06:54.602 --> 00:06:58.602
That is the greatest lesson your children can learn.

64
00:06:59.602 --> 00:07:00.602
That they will learn.

65
00:07:01.602 --> 00:07:08.602
And this also shapes the way that when Joshua goes to church on Sunday morning.

66
00:07:09.602 --> 00:07:17.602
And he sees that I treat Sunday morning as the only moment in the week that is that moment with God.

67
00:07:18.602 --> 00:07:21.602
And the rest of the week, Joshua hears nothing more about Jesus.

68
00:07:22.602 --> 00:07:24.602
It immediately sets the tone for his own life.

69
00:07:25.602 --> 00:07:28.602
So my God is my God for 7 times 24 hours.

70
00:07:29.602 --> 00:07:30.602
I am always busy with Him.

71
00:07:31.602 --> 00:07:32.602
I put Joshua to bed, I talk about God.

72
00:07:33.602 --> 00:07:36.602
We get up in the morning, we take them to school, we pray with God.

73
00:07:36.602 --> 00:07:39.602
The love of God, because God is fascinating.

74
00:07:40.602 --> 00:07:41.602
God is alive.

75
00:07:42.602 --> 00:07:43.602
God is Lord of lords.

76
00:07:44.602 --> 00:07:46.602
He is an amazing subject to talk about.

77
00:07:47.602 --> 00:07:51.602
And there is nothing so fun for Joshua to learn that language as well.

78
00:07:53.602 --> 00:07:55.602
Recently, Joshua came home.

79
00:07:56.602 --> 00:08:00.602
And he said something that this world often says.

80
00:08:01.602 --> 00:08:02.602
He is five years old.

81
00:08:03.602 --> 00:08:05.602
He said what the f said that way.

82
00:08:06.602 --> 00:08:07.602
Where did you get that from?

83
00:08:08.602 --> 00:08:11.602
Yes, from the schoolyard.

84
00:08:12.602 --> 00:08:14.602
And then you set it right immediately.

85
00:08:15.602 --> 00:08:16.602
Because this is my task.

86
00:08:17.602 --> 00:08:20.602
It is my task to say, wait a minute, that voice you hear in the schoolyard.

87
00:08:21.602 --> 00:08:22.602
My voice must be louder.

88
00:08:23.602 --> 00:08:26.602
So then you set it right immediately and you show what it means.

89
00:08:27.602 --> 00:08:30.602
And you show what a much more beautiful sound it is for Joshua.

90
00:08:31.602 --> 00:08:33.602
Namely the sound to glorify God even as a child.

91
00:08:34.602 --> 00:08:36.602
Teach them when they are young.

92
00:08:37.602 --> 00:08:40.602
Then they will also do it when they are old. Amen.

93
00:08:41.602 --> 00:08:42.602
Thank you.

94
00:09:03.602 --> 00:09:11.602
God gives instructions here to Moses to pass on to the people of Israel when they enter the promised land.

95
00:09:25.602 --> 00:09:29.602
And it is interesting because Israel is called to take possession of their promised land.

96
00:09:30.602 --> 00:09:33.602
And you are also called to take possession of your promised land.

97
00:09:40.602 --> 00:09:45.602
And God says this, so that you and your children and their children after them will learn to fear the Lord.

98
00:09:50.602 --> 00:09:54.602
As long as you live and you keep all the commandments that I give you.

99
00:09:54.602 --> 00:09:57.602
So that you can enjoy a long life.

100
00:10:03.602 --> 00:10:05.602
We all want a long and good life.

101
00:10:07.602 --> 00:10:08.602
And God shows us how.

102
00:10:10.602 --> 00:10:12.602
There is a blessing and there is a curse.

103
00:10:14.602 --> 00:10:15.602
And that is still true.

104
00:10:25.602 --> 00:10:29.602
So some people are confused and say, but this is still the Old Testament.

105
00:10:30.602 --> 00:10:33.602
But the world that does not know God still lives under that curse.

106
00:10:37.602 --> 00:10:40.602
Disobedience always brings that curse with it.

107
00:10:42.602 --> 00:10:44.602
Disobedience has consequences.

108
00:10:47.602 --> 00:10:49.602
But obedience to the Word also brings blessing.

109
00:10:50.602 --> 00:10:52.602
So there are only two things, blessing or curse.

110
00:10:58.602 --> 00:11:02.602
And even now in Christ we can choose to obey the Word of the Lord.

111
00:11:08.602 --> 00:11:10.602
So I want to read from 4 to 8 or 9.

112
00:11:13.602 --> 00:11:14.602
Listen, Israel.

113
00:11:15.602 --> 00:11:19.602
Therefore love the Lord your God with all your heart and soul and with all your strength.

114
00:11:24.602 --> 00:11:26.602
If you give everything you have to Jesus,

115
00:11:28.602 --> 00:11:30.602
then there is no room left for the world.

116
00:11:32.602 --> 00:11:33.602
Make life really simple.

117
00:11:36.602 --> 00:11:37.602
And then you can have the world.

118
00:11:37.602 --> 00:11:39.602
Then there is no room left for the world.

119
00:11:43.602 --> 00:11:44.602
Make life simple.

120
00:11:46.602 --> 00:11:47.602
Just give everything to Jesus.

121
00:11:50.602 --> 00:11:51.602
Then you have no more room for the world.

122
00:11:53.602 --> 00:11:54.602
And the influence of the world.

123
00:11:58.602 --> 00:12:01.602
Keep the commandments that I lay before you today in mind at all times.

124
00:12:04.602 --> 00:12:05.602
Impress them on your children.

125
00:12:08.602 --> 00:12:09.602
Talk about them at all times.

126
00:12:11.602 --> 00:12:12.602
At home.

127
00:12:13.602 --> 00:12:14.602
And on the road.

128
00:12:16.602 --> 00:12:17.602
So in your daily life.

129
00:12:19.602 --> 00:12:21.602
When you go to bed and when you get up again.

130
00:12:25.602 --> 00:12:28.602
Tie them as a sign on your hand and as a band on your forehead.

131
00:12:38.602 --> 00:12:42.602
Again, it should define both your thoughts and your actions.

132
00:12:42.602 --> 00:12:45.602
So it stands for your thoughts and for the things you do.

133
00:12:51.602 --> 00:12:54.602
God truly has a vision for our families and our households.

134
00:13:01.602 --> 00:13:05.602
And mom and dad represent that authority of God in a child's life.

135
00:13:08.602 --> 00:13:12.602
And we show them, as Tim said, how to love the Lord and how to follow His guidance.

136
00:13:13.602 --> 00:13:16.602
Let them see that being surrounded brings a blessing.

137
00:13:19.602 --> 00:13:21.602
And as Tim said, we teach them to love the Lord and to obey Him.

138
00:13:22.602 --> 00:13:25.602
And we show them that obedience brings blessings from God.

139
00:13:31.602 --> 00:13:32.602
Yes, that's good Vanya.

140
00:13:33.602 --> 00:13:35.602
You are doing them an injustice.

141
00:13:44.602 --> 00:13:49.602
For you are the greatest, whether you like it or not, you are, we are the greatest voice.

142
00:13:49.602 --> 00:13:53.602
We are the greatest influence and the greatest markers on our children.

143
00:13:54.602 --> 00:13:58.602
For whether you like it or not, we as parents are the greatest influence on the children.

144
00:14:08.602 --> 00:14:14.602
And the Lord wants them to be successful and He wants us to teach our children that obedience and God lead to success.

145
00:14:24.602 --> 00:14:29.602
And one of the things that becomes clear here is that there must be open communication, all day long.

146
00:14:37.602 --> 00:14:40.602
God is a God who talks to us and wants to talk to you about everything.

147
00:14:41.602 --> 00:14:43.602
And so in that way, as parents, we must represent that.

148
00:14:43.602 --> 00:14:47.602
But nothing, as Tim said about a few matters last week, nothing is off-limits.

149
00:14:49.602 --> 00:14:51.602
Nothing is taboo, nothing should remain in shame.

150
00:14:51.602 --> 00:14:54.602
In our household, you can tell us anything.

151
00:15:01.602 --> 00:15:03.602
So as parents, we must show that, as Tim said last week, nothing is taboo.

152
00:15:03.602 --> 00:15:05.602
In this household, we can talk about anything.

153
00:15:06.602 --> 00:15:07.602
So don't be ashamed.

154
00:15:07.602 --> 00:15:09.602
Did you know that God does not put us to shame?

155
00:15:14.602 --> 00:15:18.602
This is what Jesus did on the cross, He broke the power of sin and shame.

156
00:15:22.602 --> 00:15:25.602
And that is important, because shame makes you hide.

157
00:15:29.602 --> 00:15:32.602
When you are ashamed, you hide your sin.

158
00:15:33.602 --> 00:15:37.602
But even in the garden of Eden, God called out to Adam and said, I want to talk to you, where are you?

159
00:15:43.602 --> 00:15:46.602
I know where you are, but do not hide from me, come and have a conversation.

160
00:15:51.602 --> 00:15:54.602
So fathers and mothers, we must not shame our children.

161
00:15:54.602 --> 00:15:56.602
Once again, this is a learning thing.

162
00:15:56.602 --> 00:15:59.602
Especially when you have teenagers, it is important that you do not put your children to shame.

163
00:16:03.602 --> 00:16:06.602
So fathers and mothers, it is important that you do not put your children to shame.

164
00:16:06.602 --> 00:16:08.602
Especially when they are teenagers.

165
00:16:13.602 --> 00:16:16.602
How do you feel when you want to explain something and someone shames you?

166
00:16:16.602 --> 00:16:18.602
I mean, it makes you look back.

167
00:16:18.602 --> 00:16:20.602
But when someone says, you know what?

168
00:16:20.602 --> 00:16:22.602
I think it is important that you do not put your children to shame.

169
00:16:22.602 --> 00:16:24.602
Especially when you have teenagers.

170
00:16:25.602 --> 00:16:27.602
I mean, it makes you look back.

171
00:16:27.602 --> 00:16:29.602
But when someone says, you know what?

172
00:16:29.602 --> 00:16:31.602
What you are doing is not good, but I want to help you and I understand it.

173
00:16:31.602 --> 00:16:33.602
And I want to show you a way of life.

174
00:16:33.602 --> 00:16:35.602
That is what God is.

175
00:16:35.602 --> 00:16:38.602
How does it feel for you when you open up about a weakness of yours?

176
00:16:38.602 --> 00:16:42.602
And someone else who, yes, actually wants to shame you.

177
00:16:42.602 --> 00:16:48.602
While, you actually need someone who says, okay, I hear you and let me show you a new way of life.

178
00:16:48.602 --> 00:16:50.602
A spirit of religion.

179
00:16:50.602 --> 00:16:52.602
A spirit of religion.

180
00:16:53.602 --> 00:16:55.602
Make sure everyone feels guilty.

181
00:16:59.602 --> 00:17:03.602
For I have to be better than you, so I will make sure you feel guilty.

182
00:17:05.602 --> 00:17:07.602
And every sin is different.

183
00:17:11.602 --> 00:17:16.602
You struggle with things that I do not struggle with, but perhaps I struggle with things that you do not struggle with.

184
00:17:23.602 --> 00:17:31.602
So it is important with the Holy Spirit that we do not bring a cloud of shame over anyone, because it isolates them.

185
00:17:40.602 --> 00:17:48.602
So we must fight for conversations and contact that is truly face to face and not through social media, through Facebook.

186
00:17:49.602 --> 00:17:51.602
Facebook is so old.

187
00:17:53.602 --> 00:17:54.602
I have been in my role for years.

188
00:17:55.602 --> 00:17:56.602
It frees you.

189
00:17:57.602 --> 00:17:58.602
You have much more time.

190
00:18:01.602 --> 00:18:05.602
But face to face, that contact with your children is very important.

191
00:18:06.602 --> 00:18:07.602
Be present.

192
00:18:19.602 --> 00:18:23.602
It is truly an epidemic that we no longer know how to be present with attention.

193
00:18:24.602 --> 00:18:29.602
And it is important for everyone, but especially for parents. Put your phone away and pay attention to your children.

194
00:18:48.602 --> 00:19:06.602
And also in worship, it is important to keep focusing, because our generation, due to today's technology, has become accustomed to receiving things quickly and our attention span has become much shorter.

195
00:19:08.602 --> 00:19:09.602
But God is present.

196
00:19:10.602 --> 00:19:11.602
He is in the now.

197
00:19:19.602 --> 00:19:23.602
So even when you come to God, seek Him truly face to face.

198
00:19:24.602 --> 00:19:30.602
And again, everything we talk about regarding the relationship between parents and children, I relate to the relationship between us and God.

199
00:19:35.602 --> 00:19:36.602
Is this helpful?

200
00:19:37.602 --> 00:19:38.602
I think so.

201
00:19:39.602 --> 00:19:41.602
Children. I am now speaking to you.

202
00:19:42.602 --> 00:19:45.602
Children, think for yourselves. You are a child as long as you have a parent.

203
00:19:46.602 --> 00:19:49.602
Children, teenagers.

204
00:19:50.602 --> 00:19:56.602
Here is a Bible verse from Ephesians. We have already started in Ephesians and I want to read this Bible verse.

205
00:19:57.602 --> 00:20:02.602
Children, obey your parents, out of reverence for the Lord.

206
00:20:04.602 --> 00:20:08.602
For this is how it should be. Show respect for your father and your mother.

207
00:20:09.602 --> 00:20:12.602
This is the first commandment with a promise attached to it.

208
00:20:12.602 --> 00:20:17.602
For if you do this, it will go well with you and you will have a long life on earth.

209
00:20:19.602 --> 00:20:25.602
Fathers, do not embitter your children, but raise and admonish them in the training of the Lord.

210
00:20:27.602 --> 00:20:28.602
Here is the clue.

211
00:20:29.602 --> 00:20:38.602
At this moment, it is often the case that we as parents want to do everything to reassure our children.

212
00:20:38.602 --> 00:20:42.602
To calm them down. To make them happy. As long as they are doing well.

213
00:20:43.602 --> 00:20:49.602
And often children grow up in a home, and this has a sociological aspect that we are dealing with now.

214
00:20:50.602 --> 00:20:55.602
Most of us were born in a very protected environment.

215
00:20:56.602 --> 00:21:00.602
We have not seen war. We have no enemy on our doorstep.

216
00:21:01.602 --> 00:21:03.602
We have not witnessed a broken society.

217
00:21:03.602 --> 00:21:06.602
We have just come out of a global financial crisis.

218
00:21:07.602 --> 00:21:10.602
But in principle, most people were still able to keep their homes.

219
00:21:11.602 --> 00:21:12.602
Most people still had food every day.

220
00:21:13.602 --> 00:21:19.602
So most children have grown up in an economy where everything is going well.

221
00:21:20.602 --> 00:21:21.602
And why do I say this?

222
00:21:22.602 --> 00:21:31.602
I say this because it is important for a child to know that it has a place in the family to participate.

223
00:21:31.602 --> 00:21:32.602
Super important.

224
00:21:33.602 --> 00:21:38.602
Because a child that is born and experiences nothing in life,

225
00:21:39.602 --> 00:21:43.602
who thinks it has to go along with the family to keep it working,

226
00:21:44.602 --> 00:21:47.602
will ultimately become a sort of spoiled child.

227
00:21:48.602 --> 00:21:49.602
Hear me well what I am saying now.

228
00:21:50.602 --> 00:21:56.602
I am trying to explain that when the Bible says children, obey your parents,

229
00:21:56.602 --> 00:22:03.602
because there is a consequence to it that has an effect in the family and in your own life.

230
00:22:04.602 --> 00:22:05.602
And this is super important.

231
00:22:06.602 --> 00:22:11.602
