But you can also teach your children as a father what authority is.

445
00:44:35.602 --> 00:44:39.602
By also recognizing other authority yourself.

446
00:44:39.602 --> 00:44:42.602
Super important.

447
00:44:42.602 --> 00:44:48.602
If I, as a father in the family, think that I am mister number one.

448
00:44:48.602 --> 00:44:52.602
And I despise everything that has to do with the law.

449
00:44:52.602 --> 00:44:53.602
That has to do with the police.

450
00:44:53.602 --> 00:44:54.602
That has to do with taxes.

451
00:44:54.602 --> 00:44:56.602
That has to do with my wife.

452
00:44:56.602 --> 00:44:58.602
If I have been unreasonable towards her.

453
00:44:58.602 --> 00:45:00.602
Then I can stand my ground.

454
00:45:00.602 --> 00:45:02.602
Which is not according to the Bible.

455
00:45:02.602 --> 00:45:05.602
And think, I am the leader here, I am not going to say sorry to Vanessa.

456
00:45:05.602 --> 00:45:09.602
Or I show in front of my children.

457
00:45:09.602 --> 00:45:12.602
Vanessa, I am sorry for what I did today.

458
00:45:12.602 --> 00:45:13.602
I had a big mouth.

459
00:45:13.602 --> 00:45:14.602
Shall we make up?

460
00:45:14.602 --> 00:45:15.602
I give her a kiss.

461
00:45:16.602 --> 00:45:22.602
And I learn that forgiveness is part of the authority that belongs within the family.

462
00:45:22.602 --> 00:45:26.602
If Joshua and Olivia do not teach my children what forgiveness is.

463
00:45:26.602 --> 00:45:28.602
And asking for forgiveness is.

464
00:45:28.602 --> 00:45:31.602
Where are they going to learn this then?

465
00:45:31.602 --> 00:45:33.602
They will learn it nowhere.

466
00:45:33.602 --> 00:45:35.602
When I see a car passing by.

467
00:45:35.602 --> 00:45:37.602
An ambulance or a police car.

468
00:45:37.602 --> 00:45:38.602
I say this very often, why?

469
00:45:38.602 --> 00:45:40.602
I want to push this into the church.

470
00:45:40.602 --> 00:45:42.602
When I see a police car passing by with sirens.

471
00:45:42.602 --> 00:45:44.602
Then I say to Joshua, quick.

472
00:45:44.602 --> 00:45:45.602
Pray for the police.

473
00:45:45.602 --> 00:45:47.602
Because he needs wisdom at this moment.

474
00:45:47.602 --> 00:45:51.602
When I see ambulance personnel passing by with the lights on.

475
00:45:51.602 --> 00:45:52.602
Then I say, quick Joshua.

476
00:45:52.602 --> 00:45:53.602
Pray.

477
00:45:53.602 --> 00:45:55.602
Because authority is passing by here.

478
00:45:55.602 --> 00:45:58.602
Of which the Bible says that it is divine authority.

479
00:45:58.602 --> 00:46:03.602
So I, as the father of the family, must also recognize this authority.

480
00:46:03.602 --> 00:46:07.602
So that my children learn to recognize it through me.

481
00:46:07.602 --> 00:46:10.602
Can I get an amen on that?

482
00:46:11.602 --> 00:46:13.602
Okay.

483
00:46:13.602 --> 00:46:15.602
Shall we stand?

484
00:46:15.602 --> 00:46:16.602
Shall we stand?

485
00:46:16.602 --> 00:46:20.602
You know, you could talk for a whole series about upbringing.

486
00:46:20.602 --> 00:46:23.602
You could talk for ten hours about it and still not be done.

487
00:46:23.602 --> 00:46:26.602
There is one thing I want to mention very briefly.

488
00:46:26.602 --> 00:46:29.602
But I am going to pray about that now.

489
00:46:29.602 --> 00:46:32.602
Maybe I can quickly see that Bible verse after all.

490
00:46:32.602 --> 00:46:35.602
And that is Proverbs 13 verse 24.

491
00:46:35.602 --> 00:46:37.602
This is the last thing I want to say about this.

492
00:46:37.602 --> 00:46:39.602
Proverbs 13 verse 24 says this.

493
00:46:39.602 --> 00:46:43.602
He who withholds the rod from his son hates him.

494
00:46:43.602 --> 00:46:46.602
He who loves him disciplines him.

495
00:46:46.602 --> 00:46:50.602
I want to conclude this sermon with the following words.

496
00:46:50.602 --> 00:46:53.602
Often you hear in the conversation about upbringing.

497
00:46:53.602 --> 00:46:57.602
Whether you can give your child a smack or whether you should not give your child a smack.

498
00:46:57.602 --> 00:46:59.602
To hit or not to hit.

499
00:46:59.602 --> 00:47:03.602
And I think if I were to take a vote on this.

500
00:47:03.602 --> 00:47:06.602
That 70% would say you should not hit your child.

501
00:47:06.602 --> 00:47:09.602
And 30% would say, well, a healthy smack.

502
00:47:09.602 --> 00:47:12.602
What I want to establish here is this.

503
00:47:12.602 --> 00:47:15.602
I think you should not hit your children, period.

504
00:47:15.602 --> 00:47:18.602
So that's one voice, that way.

505
00:47:18.602 --> 00:47:21.602
I think you should not hit your children.

506
00:47:21.602 --> 00:47:23.602
But what the Bible says here.

507
00:47:23.602 --> 00:47:25.602
He who withholds the rod hates him.

508
00:47:25.602 --> 00:47:26.602
This is indeed contextual.

509
00:47:26.602 --> 00:47:31.602
This is from a time when there was a law.

510
00:47:32.602 --> 00:47:35.602
In the Old Testament, it was eye for eye, tooth for tooth.

511
00:47:35.602 --> 00:47:37.602
If you steal, your hand gets cut off.

512
00:47:37.602 --> 00:47:39.602
Corporal punishment was very normal back then.

513
00:47:39.602 --> 00:47:44.602
So you see that generations of societies and economies arise.

514
00:47:44.602 --> 00:47:47.602
Where it says, okay, if you have hit your sister.

515
00:47:47.602 --> 00:47:49.602
Then come here, and I will hit you on your hand.

516
00:47:49.602 --> 00:47:51.602
So that you can no longer hit your sister.

517
00:47:51.602 --> 00:47:55.602
All these kinds of parenting concepts exist.

518
00:47:55.602 --> 00:47:57.602
Do you know what I want to say about that?

519
00:47:57.602 --> 00:48:00.602
You need God on how to raise your child.

520
00:48:00.602 --> 00:48:05.602
You urgently, urgently need the guidance of the Holy Spirit.

521
00:48:05.602 --> 00:48:07.602
Because, here we go again.

522
00:48:07.602 --> 00:48:10.602
You can watch a thousand videos on YouTube.

523
00:48:10.602 --> 00:48:12.602
How to raise your child.

524
00:48:12.602 --> 00:48:14.602
And there are many psychologists today.

525
00:48:14.602 --> 00:48:18.602
Who really have a lot of good wisdom about it.

526
00:48:18.602 --> 00:48:23.602
But there are also many psychologists that I look at today.

527
00:48:23.602 --> 00:48:27.602
Who all spout nonsense about children and parenting.

528
00:48:28.602 --> 00:48:31.602
Deadly nonsense.

529
00:48:31.602 --> 00:48:35.602
Bad stuff about parenting.

530
00:48:35.602 --> 00:48:38.602
So it is also quite difficult to define sometimes.

531
00:48:38.602 --> 00:48:40.602
What is wisdom?

532
00:48:40.602 --> 00:48:42.602
And what should I do and what should I not do?

533
00:48:42.602 --> 00:48:45.602
And I want to deliberately not bring up those kinds of things in this sermon, at the end of this sermon.

534
00:48:45.602 --> 00:48:48.602
Whether you should hit your child or not.

535
00:48:48.602 --> 00:48:50.602
Or whether you should put them in the corner.

536
00:48:50.602 --> 00:48:52.602
Or whether you should put them in the hallway.

537
00:48:52.602 --> 00:48:54.602
Because if you put them in the hallway, that can lead to too much isolation.

538
00:48:54.602 --> 00:48:57.602
No, you should put them in the corner, in the room where everyone is present.

539
00:48:57.602 --> 00:49:01.602
Or you should take them to their room.

540
00:49:01.602 --> 00:49:03.602


541
00:49:03.602 --> 00:49:05.602
Or you have to send them to bed early without food.

542
00:49:05.602 --> 00:49:10.602
There are thousands, thousands, thousands of parenting techniques.

543
00:49:10.602 --> 00:49:14.602
Of which it is said, this is the only true truth.

544
00:49:14.602 --> 00:49:20.602
My truth is that I need to lean into the Holy Spirit every day again.

545
00:49:20.602 --> 00:49:23.602
And ask Him how I should raise my children.

546
00:49:23.602 --> 00:49:27.602
Because you know, Joshua needs to be raised differently than Olivia.

547
00:49:27.602 --> 00:49:29.602
He needs a different approach.

548
00:49:29.602 --> 00:49:34.602
And the Father in heaven knows exactly how I should approach Joshua.

549
00:49:34.602 --> 00:49:38.602
The Father in heaven knows exactly how I should approach my daughter.

550
00:49:38.602 --> 00:49:39.602
Amen?

551
00:49:39.602 --> 00:49:41.602
Can we close our eyes?

552
00:49:41.602 --> 00:49:43.602
Because I want to pray for this topic.

553
00:49:43.602 --> 00:49:45.602
Vanessa, would you please do that?

554
00:49:47.602 --> 00:49:48.602
Thank you.

555
00:49:49.602 --> 00:49:57.602
Father, we ask this morning that you impart your wisdom upon us.

556
00:49:57.602 --> 00:50:04.602
That this does not just remain knowledge, but that it truly becomes part of us.

557
00:50:04.602 --> 00:50:13.602
I pray that this will truly transform the way we interact with our children.

558
00:50:13.602 --> 00:50:22.602
And I pray for mothers and fathers that they will hear the Holy Spirit for their children.

559
00:50:22.602 --> 00:50:30.602
That the things they have heard today, they can turn into action.

560
00:50:30.602 --> 00:50:35.602
And I speak a blessing over parents.

561
00:50:35.602 --> 00:50:38.602
That you will have wisdom.

562
00:50:38.602 --> 00:50:40.602
And understanding.

563
00:50:40.602 --> 00:50:47.602
And that you will have perseverance with your parents.

564
00:50:47.602 --> 00:50:48.602
In your parenthood.

565
00:50:48.602 --> 00:50:49.602
In Jesus' name.

566
00:50:49.602 --> 00:50:50.602
In Jesus' name.

567
00:50:50.602 --> 00:50:51.602
And everyone says?

568
00:50:51.602 --> 00:50:52.602
Amen.
